","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2016","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2015","make":"CADILLAC","model":"ESCALADE"},{"year":"2015","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2015","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2017","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2017","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2017","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2016","make":"CADILLAC","model":"ESCALADE"},{"year":"2016","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2016","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2017","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2016","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2016","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2017","make":"CADILLAC","model":"ESCALADE"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2017","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"19V761000","received":"2019-10-24","manufacturer":"General Motors LLC","component":"SERVICE BRAKES, HYDRAULIC:ANTILOCK/TRACTION CONTROL/ELECTRONIC LIMITED SLIP:WHEEL SPEED SENSOR/TONE RING","summary":"General Motors LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2015-2020 Chevrolet Suburban, Tahoe, and GMC Yukon, and 2014-2018 Chevrolet Silverado 1500 and GMC Sierra 1500 vehicles equipped with a 5.3-liter engine, a 3.08-ratio rear axle and four-wheel drive.  If a wheel-speed sensor fails, while the vehicle is traveling between 41 and 60 mph in four-wheel or automatic mode, the Electronic-Brake Control Module (EBCM) software may activate the driveline-protection system.","consequence":"Unintended activation of the driveline-protection system will cause unintended braking on the wheel on the opposite side of the failed sensor, causing the vehicle to pull to one side unexpectedly, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"GM will notify owners, and dealers will reprogram the EBCM, free of charge.  The recall began December 11, 2019.  Owners may contact Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-630-2438 or GMC customer service at 1-800-462-8782.  GM's number for this recall is N192261050.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":652967,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V761000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":28,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2014","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2014","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2016","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2015","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2015","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2017","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2017","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2017","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2016","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2016","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2017","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2016","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2016","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2017","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2020","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2020","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SUBURBAN"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"20V603000","received":"2020-10-01","manufacturer":"General Motors LLC","component":"SERVICE BRAKES, HYDRAULIC:POWER ASSIST:VACUUM","summary":"General Motors LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2018 Cadillac Escalade, Chevrolet Silverado 1500 and Tahoe, GMC Sierra 1500 and Yukon vehicles equipped with either a 5.3L or 6.2L V8 engine.  The output of the mechanical vacuum pump can decrease over time, decreasing the amount of vacuum/power brake assist.","consequence":"A decrease in brake assist can increase the brake pedal effort and distance required to stop the vehicle, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"GM will notify owners, and dealers will reprogram the Electronic Brake Control Module, free of charge.  The recall began November 11, 2020.  Owners may contact GM customer service at 1-866-522-9559, Cadillac customer service at 1-800-458-8006 or Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-630-2438.  GM's number for this recall is N202300860.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":14620,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=20V603000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":5,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"TAHOE"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"YUKON"},{"year":"2018","make":"CADILLAC","model":"ESCALADE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"24V756000","received":"2024-10-10","manufacturer":"General Motors, LLC","component":"AIR BAGS:SIDE/WINDOW:CURTAIN:INFLATOR","summary":"General Motors, LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2018 Chevrolet Silverado 1500, GMC Sierra 1500, 2018-2019 Chevrolet Silverado 2500, 3500, and GMC Sierra 2500, 3500 Crew Cab trucks.  The left or right-side roof-rail air bag (RRAB) inflator end cap may detach from the inflator or the inflator sidewall may rupture.","consequence":"A separated inflator end cap or inflator rupture can allow compressed gas to escape, resulting in the end cap or other components being propelled into the vehicle, increasing the risk of injury or crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the left and right side RRAB modules, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed November 8, 2024.  Owners may contact Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-222-1020, and GMC Customer Service at 888-988-7267.  GM's number for this recall is N242474500.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":2061,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=24V756000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":10,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 3500"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 2500"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 3500"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 2500"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 2500"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 3500"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 2500"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 3500"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"25V432000","received":"2025-06-26","manufacturer":"General Motors, LLC","component":"AIR BAGS","summary":"General Motors (GM) is recalling certain 2018 GMC Sierra 1500, 2019 Sierra 2500, 3500, Chevrolet Silverado 3500, and Chevrolet Silverado 2500 and 2018 Chevrolet Silverado 1500 Crew Cab vehicles. The left or right-side roof-rail air bag (RRAB) inflator end cap may detach from the inflator or the inflator sidewall may rupture.","consequence":"A detached end cap or inflator rupture can allow compressed gas to escape and project the end cap or fragments of the inflator into the vehicle, increases the risk of injury or crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the left and right side RRAB modules, free of charge. Owner notification letters were mailed July 23, 2025. Owners may contact GMC customer service at 1-888-988-7267 or Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-222-1020. GM's number for this recall is N252513060.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":1658,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=25V432000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":6,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 3500"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 2500"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 3500"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 2500"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"26V166000","received":"2026-03-19","manufacturer":"General Motors, LLC","component":"AIR BAGS","summary":"General Motors, LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2018 Chevrolet Silverado 1500, GMC Sierra 1500, 2019 Chevrolet Silverado 2500, Silverado 3500, GMC Sierra 2500, and Sierra 3500 Crew Cab vehicles.  The left or right-side roof rail air bag (RRAB) inflator end cap may detach from the inflator or the inflator sidewall may rupture.","consequence":"A detached end cap or inflator rupture can allow compressed gas to escape and project the end cap or fragments of the inflator into the vehicle, increasing the risk of injury.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the left and right-side RRAB modules, free of charge. Owner notification letters were mailed April 16, 2026. Owners may contact GMC customer service at 1-888-988-7267 or Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-222-1020. GM's number for this recall is N262549710. Vehicle Identification Numbers (VINs) involved in this recall became searchable on NHTSA.gov on March 19, 2026.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":2819,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=26V166000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":6,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 2500"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 3500"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 2500"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 3500"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"26V325000","received":"2026-05-21","manufacturer":"General Motors, LLC","component":"AIR BAGS","summary":"General Motors, LLC (GM) is recalling certain 2018 Chevrolet Silverado 1500, GMC Sierra 1500, 2019 Chevrolet Silverado 2500, Silverado 3500, GMC Sierra 2500, and Sierra 3500 vehicles. The left-side or right-side roof rail air bag (RRAB) inflator end cap may detach from the inflator or the inflator sidewall may rupture.","consequence":"A detached end cap or inflator rupture can allow compressed gas to escape and project the end cap or fragments of the inflator into the vehicle, increasing the risk of injury.","remedy":"Dealers will replace both RRAB modules, free of charge. Owner notification letters were mailed June 24, 2026. Owners may contact GMC customer service at 1-888-988-7267 or Chevrolet customer service at 1-800-222-1020. GM's number for this recall is N262557310. Vehicle Identification Numbers (VINs) involved in this recall became searchable on NHTSA.gov on May 21, 2026. This recall expands previous NHTSA recall number 26V166.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":4315,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=26V325000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":6,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 3500"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 2500"},{"year":"2019","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 3500"},{"year":"2019","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 2500"},{"year":"2018","make":"CHEVROLET","model":"SILVERADO 1500"},{"year":"2018","make":"GMC","model":"SIERRA 1500"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false}]}
